# Original explanation of the owning evidence-indirectness example.
# The central question is an evidence gap, not a proven mechanism.
direction: down
study: "Studied question\nshort-term surrogate"
finding: "Observed result\nfor that surrogate"
bridge: "Connection to target\nestablished?"
bridge.shape: diamond
target: "Target question\nlong-term functioning"
study -> finding: study reports
finding -> bridge: needs appraisal
target -> bridge: asks a different outcome
